This directory covers several licenses -- one per DLL shipped inside the
gawk payload. `LICENSE` is an index; the full canonical texts are the
LICENSE-*.txt files beside it (see PROVENANCE.md for the DLL-to-license
mapping).

  libreadline8.dll      -> LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt
                           (GNU GPL v3; readline is GPL-3.0-or-later)
  libgmp-10.dll         -> LICENSE-LGPL-3.0.txt and LICENSE-GPL-2.0.txt
                           (GMP's standard dual license: LGPL-3.0 / GPL-2.0)
  libmpfr-6.dll         -> LICENSE-LGPL-3.0.txt
  libncurses6.dll       -> LICENSE-NCURSES.txt
                           (MIT-style ncurses COPYRIGHT NOTICE)
  libgcc_s_dw2-1.dll    -> LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt together with
                           LICENSE-GCC-RUNTIME-EXCEPTION-3.1.txt
                           (GPL-3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception)

The exception file applies to libgcc only, in combination with the GPL v3
text; it is not a standalone license. The GPL-2.0 text applies to libgmp
only, as the second alternative of its dual license.

The ncurses notice must accompany the distribution and its documentation;
staging this directory into the archive as `licenses\dll-closure\`
satisfies that requirement.
